---
/**
 * /ai-and-data-use — plain-language statement of how Cedar uses data.
 *
 * A working draft in the site's register for counsel to review,
 * recommended in docs/legal/legal-framework-review.md Part 4 as a
 * sales asset for government and Tribal customers. Every claim here
 * is derived from positions the Terms and Privacy Policy already
 * take; nothing states a provider-contract or architecture detail
 * that has not been verified. The provider and subprocessor
 * disclosures are deliberately written as "to be published" until
 * the internal data-flow specification exists (roadmap item 9) —
 * this page must never run ahead of it.
 */
import { site } from '../config';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="AI and Data Use | Lumecon"
  description="How Cedar, Lumecon's AI economic analyst, uses data: what it reads, what it never does, and how your organization's content is handled across the Cedar product family."
  canonical="https://lumecon.ai/ai-and-data-use"
  keywords="Lumecon AI policy, Cedar AI data use, AI data handling, government AI procurement, tribal data sovereignty, economic analysis AI"
>
  <h1>AI and Data Use</h1>
  <div class="date">Working draft, under review by counsel.</div>

  <p>
    Lumecon is the intelligent economic analysis platform, and Cedar is the AI economic analyst
    inside it. This page says in plain language what Cedar does with data, what it never does, and
    what is still being formalized. It exists because our customers, governments, Tribal
    Nations, universities and the organizations that answer to them, are accountable for the
    tools they bring in, and deserve answers before a procurement review has to ask.
  </p>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">1. Where AI sits in the platform</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Cedar works across the Cedar product family: it reads the documents you bring into Cedar
        Impact, helps structure them into model-ready inputs, surfaces gaps and assumptions for your
        sign-off, and helps turn results into reporting. AI in the workflow, economists in the loop:
        the economic model itself is deterministic input-output economics, not a language model, and
        every figure an analysis produces comes from the model with a lineage you can inspect. Cedar
        assists the work; it does not invent the numbers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">2. What Cedar reads, and why</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        In the product, Cedar processes the content your organization brings to its analyses:
        budgets, financial statements, payroll and program records, in the documents and figures you
        upload. It reads them to do the job you asked for: interpreting documents, mapping them
        into the model, flagging assumptions and drafting language you review. Your content is used
        to run your analyses and support you, as the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> states.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">3. What we do not do</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information, and we do not use your information for third-party
        advertising. Improvement work uses aggregated and de-identified information and does not
        identify you or your organization. Cedar drafts and suggests; it does not approve its own
        work: assumptions are surfaced for a person&rsquo;s sign-off, and economic judgment
        stays human.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">4. Cedar on this website</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        The chat on lumecon.ai is a lightweight Cedar that answers questions about Lumecon. On the
        static site it is answered by a local classifier running in your browser and sends nothing
        to an AI provider; where a backend is configured, the conversation is processed to answer
        you and reviewed in aggregate to improve the answers. Either way, it is not connected to any
        customer&rsquo;s product data, and you should not put sensitive information in a chat.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">5. AI providers and subprocessors</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Where Cedar relies on third-party AI providers, we are putting written contracts governing
        the use of customer data in place with each of them, and we will not represent those
        protections as final until they are verified. A plain-language summary of the provider
        relationships and a subprocessor list will be published on this page as they are finalized;
        we would rather this section say &ldquo;coming&rdquo; than say more than the signed
        contracts do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">6. Data sovereignty</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Your content belongs to your organization. For Tribal Nations and government customers this
        is more than a licensing term: data governance is a design priority, publicity opt-outs are
        honored, and analyses are your record to keep, share or withhold. If your government or
        procurement process needs specific commitments in writing, ask us; that is a
        conversation we expect and welcome.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="legal-sec">
    <summary><h2 class="legal-subhead">7. Questions</h2></summary>
    <div class="legal-sec__body">
      <p>
        Write to <a class="note-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and a person will
        answer. This page will be kept consistent with the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> as counsel finalizes them, and updated here with a new date
        when it changes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Counsel:</strong>{' '}{site.counsel}<br />Contact: <a
      href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
      class="note-link">{site.email}</a
    >
  </div>
</LegalLayout>
